<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The integrator and the analytical eigenvalue are unchanged from pass 1. Pass 2 measures growth on the exact dorsoventral DFT modes of the window, which are the eigenfunctions of the discrete Laplacian the solver uses. gamma remains a scale calibration rather than a transcribed Nakamasu parameter." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "On the 11 exact modes, Pearson r = 0.9805 and RMSE = 0.0191. The KS statistic is 0.273 against a ceiling of 0.40, so the pass-1 coincidence of D with its own reference is gone. GIF coherency 0.4399 is not the specimen coherency 0.3887, and the predecessor wavelength is 20.64 µm against the rerio target 24.08 µm. The correlation clears 0.98 with little room; one low-k mode still sits off the analytical curve." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-curve-pearson-r-of-pde-growth-versus-analytical-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse-between-analytical-and-numerical-growth-rates>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-negative-control-field-amplitude>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-kolmogorov-smirnov-statistic-of-analytical-versus-numerical-growth-rate-samples>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-predecessor-danio-nigrofasciatus-dominant-wavelength-at-anisotropy-1-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-segmented-specimen-foreground-fraction-versus-gif-occupancy>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-selected-dorsoventral-wavelength-of-the-holocene-danio-rerio-field>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-tensor-coherency-of-the-rendered-gif>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 86.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg system (a=0.11, b=1.24, Du=0.80, Dv_y=20.80, gamma=0.1989, anisotropy 3.85). The GIF pigment is now a steep sigmoid of the activator, colored with the specimen dark and light palette, and the comparison figure shows that fish-mask composite beside the photograph. Dispersion growth rates are measured on the 11 exact dorsoventral Fourier modes: Pearson r = 0.9805, RMSE = 0.0191, KS D = 0.273 against a 0.40 ceiling. Selected wavelength remains 24.08 µm. Computer-vision similarity of the 960×540, 12-frame GIF against the photograph is 77.8. Overall 86.5/100 (faithfulness 85.1, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 87, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 386615 B, 1716×924 px, artifact_sha256 71b3259f10bb6add771cc22f7329df46c530d873ced69f4a8c730d9e4eef9dae (sha256 71b3259f10bb6add771cc22f7329df46c530d873ced69f4a8c730d9e4eef9dae), spec_fingerprint d7d1a6ee4915a8532ac3ba145d5dd7b6436e0f7006bd83ec8bd0ab39b939e0f7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d7d1a6ee4915a8532ac3ba145d5dd7b6436e0f7006bd83ec8bd0ab39b939e0f7; artifact_sha256: 71b3259f10bb6add771cc22f7329df46c530d873ced69f4a8c730d9e4eef9dae; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=dbe49b6901b94381..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_rerio_specimen.jpg=850b2d4a94c7cbcb..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=8456a78d5a6e1822..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=e77f417b131e9ec8..., datasets/danio_rerio_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=7dfbf8b27236cb36...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: two-species reaction-diffusion selects a critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: zebrafish melanophores and xanthophores are a short-range activation / long-range inhibition pair. | Hiscock & Megason 2015: anisotropy orients stripes by removing one axis from the unstable band. | Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: D. nigrofasciatus is broken-striped or spotted relative to D. rerio.; reconstructed_in_script: Anisotropic Schnakenberg integration on a 288.96 × 144.48 µm window with Dv_y/Dv_x = 3.85 for D. rerio and 1.12 for the predecessor. | Growth-rate comparison on exact y-DFT modes, anisotropy sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, and three noise seeds. | Specimen mask segmentation and a bimodal pigment composite of the simulated field.; transfer_boundary: The 144.48 µm cellular window is magnified onto the adult outline. Adult stripes are not 24.08 µm wide. | gamma is calibrated so the dispersion peak lies on the assigned scale.; does_not_claim: That the gray-brown composite reproduces iridophore iridescence or the eye. | That the predecessor was measured at 24.08 µm; the contrast is the anisotropy mechanism at this assigned scale. | A cryptographic nanopublication signature.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Nanopubs are unsigned because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.",
        "remediation needed: No second assessor has scored this pass.",
        "remediation needed: The composite has no eye and no iridescent blue; the stripe count is the cellular window, not the adult flank.",
        "remediation needed: gamma = 0.1989 is calibrated to the assigned 24.08 µm scale rather than copied from a published table." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.65e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 2) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Gradient anisotropy rises monotonically across inhibitor ratios 1.12, 2.0, 3.85, and 6.0 (about 1.2 to 6.0). The predecessor sits at the isotropic end and the equal-diffusion ablation stays at numerical roundoff. The sweep is the same experiment as pass 1 and is plotted with both chronospecies marked." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-rerio-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio rerio Holocene 24.08 µm anisotropic Schnakenberg wavelength (pass 2) — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "--self-test still requires Pearson r > 0.98, RMSE < 0.02, wavelength error below 0.75 µm, a dead equal-diffusion control, three seeds, a rising anisotropy sweep, and a GIF of at least 10 frames and 480 px. The pass-2 command completes in about 11 s from a fixed seed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
